module test.claim.deployment_gate_operator_steps_witness

// Witness file for the five operator acts that stand up the deployment gate, and for the ordering that
// keeps the gate shut until the app-side rule has been witnessed BOTH ways.
//
// WHY THESE TESTS ARE NOT IN gunbc.auth.deployment_gate_operator_steps. No module under dag/gunbc/auth
// carries a test on main, and the reason is worth stating: a production module that ships fixtures
// ships values someone can mistake for observations. The removal act is guarded by a typed admission;
// if the evidence inside that admission were a fixture sitting in the module the act is decided from,
// the guard would be the prose it replaced wearing a type. So the fixtures live here, and — for the
// trial evidence specifically — they are not literals either: they are minted through the readback fold
// that GitHub's own records feed.
//
// Each test below is written so the WRONG model returns the wrong answer. The ordering control is
// exercised by performing the swap a shortcut would make; the identity census by dropping and doubling
// a row; the permission census by widening the App by one axis; the readback control by citing the
// endpoint that cannot answer the question.

